  "text_pages": [
    "Housing in Strasbourg - International Welcome e-desk - University of Strasbourg\nShare the page :\nAdd the page to your favorites :\nPage has been added to favorites\nPage has been removed from favorites\nHousing in Strasbourg\nStart looking for accommodation as soon as possible!\nFinding accommodation in large French cities takes time. To increase your chances:\nPlan your accommodation search\nat least 2 to 3 months before your arrival in Strasbourg;\nWork out your budget and\napply for financial support\nif necessary;\nFind out\nwhere to look for accommodation\n.\nHave you found the ad that suits you? Find out what you need to do\nbefore moving in\n.\nHave you signed your lease? Here are some tips to help you\nsettle into your new home.\nYour lease is nearing its end and you're about to leave Strasbourg. Here are some final tips to help you\norganize your departure.\nPlanning Your Housing Search\nPlan your housing search by identifying your needs and assessing your financial resources.\nHousing Benefits\nFinancial support for your housing search, move or monthly rent.\nHousing Search\nThere is a wide range of resources to help you in your housing search: real estate agencies, ads, university residences, accommodation guides, \"zoom logement\" information sessions.\nMoving in\nAll the steps you need to take before moving in: walk-through inspection, lease,...\nLiving in the Accomodation\nAll the information you need to equip and maintain your home, to recycle and be a good neighbour.\nMoving Out\nAll the steps you need to take while and after moving out.\nRead more\nHow do I find accommodation in Strasbourg?\nThe search for accommodation in Strasbourg, as in all major university towns, should begin\nas early as possible\n.\nFurther information:\n'Housing'\nIf you are studying at the University of Strasbourg as\npart of an exchange programme\n, you can\napply for accommodation in a Crous residence\nwhen you apply online.\nIn other cases,\naccommodation information sessions (\"Zoom logement\")\nare organised by videoconference throughout the year.\nFurther information: '\nPreparing your housing search'\nThe University of Strasbourg offers accommodation solutions for doctoral students and international researchers and lecturers:\nThe European Doctoral College (Collège doctoral européen)\nwelcomes newcomers doctoral students in joint PhD.\nThe Villa Arconati Visconti\nis reserved for teachers, researchers and post-doctoral students for stays from one week to a maximum of 3 months.\nFurther information: '\nPreparing your housing search'\nMenu\nBrowse those links to navigate the website\nDisplay\nHide\nthe searchbox\nFill in your search :\nLaunch search\nClose\nOur audiences :\nStudent Profile\nResearcher Profile\nI think about it\nBefore\nmy arrival\nI am\nin\nStrasbourg\nBefore\nmy departure\nServices Pack"
  ],
